{"skill":{"slug":"facebook","displayName":"Facebook"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1770028711580,"changelog":"Version 1.0.1\n\n- Expanded documentation with six new reference files covering Graph API overview, Page posting, comments moderation, permissions/tokens, webhooks, and HTTP request examples.\n- Updated guidance to focus on direct HTTPS requests for Facebook Pages: posting, comment management, and Page operations.\n- Clarified required inputs (App ID/Secret, Page ID, token strategy).\n- Added detailed security and operational guardrails.\n- Clearly defined recommended use cases and limitations.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1688,"sha256":"0de00402c01527ea2f9a0e3c8479f1274397a2b29b627a039ad72d9c02d84db9","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/permissions-and-tokens.md","size":719,"sha256":"b3f8dbde96f5a3a1944f9439ba9108946b5d4e9884ff24b00a1906492c1892b8","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/comments-moderation.md","size":625,"sha256":"f1b240bc5b0536b19b1cbd00d2e3183c1e3ae603796c675f5bfbf82a0683eb4d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/webhooks.md","size":519,"sha256":"3f706693319a819ce8b0e19414a1e46a12a89c3262bd21e5fd3c38b58e494ab2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/graph-api-overview.md","size":810,"sha256":"e82d828c0bf559b791ff6691f1b614e4eb25b1da3824898433a53bb4dd0a5eee","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/page-posting.md","size":918,"sha256":"66272b73f36f52e3740fa724d00109d0feb1535ef173502bc787e4fa7a459eac","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/http-request-templates.md","size":762,"sha256":"66449ce3aeb80e4456b03c19a1a4723daedc7bb49b47fbbada129c11e26c7955","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2442,"sha256":"1a494b74bfeff5f34cde335467901e9934e291c429e90f47dbd2ef02996b057d","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789026854320,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a22e25b9fe764d54e5cfe6d72f41a232da2783a1c2669b1f46960a1b11698567","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a22e25b9fe764d54e5cfe6d72f41a232da2783a1c2669b1f46960a1b11698567","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: facebook\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill bundle consists entirely of documentation files (`.md`) providing guidance on using the Facebook Graph API for Page management. There is no executable code, and the `SKILL.md` instructions for the AI agent are purely informational, aligning with the stated purpose. The content explicitly advises against logging tokens or app secrets, and there are no indicators of prompt injection, data exfiltration, malicious execution, or other high-risk behaviors across any of the files.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160712040},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":76,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":13,"checkedAt":1789026854320},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This Facebook Graph API skill is a coherent documentation-only guide, but it gives agents live Page posting, deletion, moderation, and token-handling guidance without enough guardrails around irreversible or public actions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Direct HTTPS use and OAuth/Page tokens are proportionate for Facebook Page workflows, but the skill also permits access tokens in URL query parameters, which expands leakage risk.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact contains Markdown documentation only; no executable install scripts, dependencies, or hidden runtime payloads were found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill documents live publish, update, hide, and delete operations but does not consistently require explicit user confirmation, target verification, or safer dry-run/read-only checks before public or destructive actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No local persistence or privilege escalation is present, but the documented Page access token workflows can authorize high-impact mutations to public Page content and comments.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Facebook Page publishing, comment moderation, and Page management, and the referenced API operations match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with an agent helping operate live Facebook Pages. Require the agent to use Authorization headers, never URL token parameters, and insist on explicit confirmation before publishing, editing, hiding, or deleting posts or comments.","findings":"[TM1] expected: The DELETE post/comment endpoints are legitimate Facebook Page management operations, not tool-parameter abuse by themselves; the concern is the lack of confirmation and irreversibility warnings.\n[PE3] expected: References to user and Page access tokens are expected for Graph API workflows and do not show credential-file access or theft in the artifact.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The scanner concern is supported: public posting, hiding, and deletion examples are documented without nearby warnings or required confirmation steps.\n[T09] unexpected: The artifact explicitly allows access tokens in query parameters as an alternative to Authorization headers, which is avoidable sensitive credential exposure risk.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789026854320}}}}}